d_embed_dim": 20,\n  "adaptive_embedding_dim": 0,\n  "lamb_c": 0.01,\n  "lamb_d": 1.0,\n  "steps": [50, 70]\n}\n```\n\n### PEMS-BAY (325 nodes)\n```json\n{\n  "input_embedding_dim": 10,\n  "node_embedding_dim": 20,\n  "tod_embed_dim": 20,\n  "adaptive_embedding_dim": 0,\n  "lamb_c": 0.01,\n  "lamb_d": 1.0,\n  "cl_decay_steps": 8000,\n  "steps": [10, 70, 150]\n}\n```\n\n### PEMS04 (307 nodes)\n```json\n{\n  "rnn_units": 32,\n  "input_embedding_dim": 32,\n  "node_embedding_dim": 24,\n  "tod_embed_dim": 40,\n  "lamb_c": 0.01,\n  "lamb_d": 0.01,\n  "cl_decay_steps": 6000,\n  "learning_rate": 0.001,\n  "batch_size": 16\n}\n```\n\n## Data Requirements\n\n### Standard LibCity Format\n- Input: `(batch, time_in, num_nodes, features)`\n- Features: [speed, time-of-day, (optional) historical]\n- Time-of-day normalized to [0, 1]\n\n### Optimal Performance (with Historical Anchors)\nFor best results, preprocess data to include weekly historical averages:\n\n```bash\n# Navigate to ST-SSDL repository\ncd repos/ST-SSDL\n\n# Generate historical anchors for METR-LA\npython generate_training_data_his_LA.py --dataset METRLA\n\n# Generate for PEMS-BAY\npython generate_training_data_his_BAY.py --dataset PEMSBAY\n\n# This creates train/val/test his.npz files with 3 channels:\n# Channel 0: current speed\n# Channel 1: time-of-day\n# Channel 2: historical weekly average\n```\n\n## Model Components\n\n### 1. Encoder\n- Adaptive Graph Convolutional RNN (AGCRN)\n- Processes current and historical sequences\n- Outputs hidden states for prototype querying\n\n### 2. Prototype Module\n- 20 learnable prototypes (traffic patterns)\n- Query mechanism: select top-2 similar prototypes\n- Computes deviation between current and historical\n\n### 3. Decoder\n- Autoregressive generation\n- Uses adaptive graph (learned from hidden states)\n- Curriculum learning for training\n\n### 4. Loss Function\n```\nTotal Loss = MAE + λ_c × Contrastive + λ_d × Deviation\n```\n- **MAE:** Prediction accuracy\n- **Contrastive:** Triplet margin loss (distinguish prototypes)\n- **Deviation:** L1 between latent and prototype distances\n\n## Expected Performance\n\n| Dataset   | MAE  | RMSE | MAPE   |\n|-----------|------|------|--------|\n| METR-LA   | 2.88 | 5.67 | 7.50%  |\n| PEMS-BAY  | 1.37 | 2.88 | 2.95%  |\n| PEMS04    | 19.26| 31.48| 12.85% |\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Issue: Low performance\n**Solution:** Ensure historical anchor data is available (3rd feature channel)\n\n### Issue: Out of memory\n**Solution:** Reduce `rnn_units`, `prototype_num`, or embedding dimensions\n\n### Issue: Unstable training\n**Solution:** Adjust `lamb_c` and `lamb_d` weights (try 0.01 for both)\n\n### Issue: Slow convergence\n**Solution:**\n- Check learning rate (try 0.001 for larger datasets)\n- Adjust `cl_decay_steps` (increase for more gradual curriculum)\n\n## Advanced Configuration\n\n### Disable Spatio-Temporal Embeddings\n```json\n{\n  "use_STE": false,\n  "input_embedding_dim": 0,\n  "node_embedding_dim": 0,\n  "tod_embed_dim": 0,\n  "adaptive_embedding_dim": 0\n}\n```\n\n### Disable Curriculum Learning\n```json\n{\n  "use_curriculum_learning": false\n}\n```\n\n### Change Contrastive Loss\n```json\n{\n  "contra_loss": "triplet",  // or "infonce"\n  "margin": 0.5              // for triplet loss\n}\n```\n\n## Python API Example\n\n```python\nfrom libcity.config import ConfigParser\nfrom libcity.data import get_dataset\nfrom libcity.model import STSSDL\nfrom libcity.executor import TrafficStateExecutor\n\n# Configuration\nconfig = ConfigParser(\n    task=\'traffic_state_pred\',\n    model=\'STSSDL\',\n    dataset=\'METR_LA\',\n    config_file=\'libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/STSSDL.json\'\n)\n\n# Override parameters\nconfig[\'lamb_c\'] = 0.01\nconfig[\'lamb_d\'] = 1.0\nconfig[\'rnn_units\'] = 128\n\n# Load data\ndataset = get_dataset(config)\ndata_feature = dataset.get_data_feature()\n\n# Initialize model\nmodel = STSSDL(config, data_feature)\n\n# Train\nexecutor = TrafficStateExecutor(config, model, dataset)\nexecutor.train()\n\n# Evaluate\nresults = executor.evaluate()\nprint(results)\n```\n\n## Monitoring Training\n\n### Check Loss Components\nAdd to config:\n```json\n{\n  "log_level": "DEBUG"\n}\n```\n\nThis will show individual loss components:\n```\nMAE: 3.45, Contrastive: 0.12, Deviation: 0.08\n```\n\n### Visualize Prototypes\nAfter training, access learned prototypes:\n```python\nprototypes = model.model.prototypes[\'prototypes\']\nprint(prototypes.shape)  # (20, 64)\n```\n\n## Citation\n\nIf you use this model, please cite:\n```bibtex\n@inproceedings{stssdl2025,\n  title={How Different from the Past? Self-Supervised Deviation Learning for Spatio-Temporal Time Series Forecasting},\n  author={[Authors]},\n  booktitle={NeurIPS},\n  year={2025}\n}\n```\n\n## Support\n\n- Full documentation: `STSSDL_ADAPTATION_REPORT.md`\n- LibCity issues: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity/issues\n- Model file: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/STSSDL.py`\n'}

